From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:59:33 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 47/48] Meridian: no dark flash switching spaces in fullscreen;
 history swipe works

Spaces in another profile live in their own window. In native fullscreen,
hiding the shown window closed its macOS Space, so every switch went through
a dark transition. Now the other window is shown over the fullscreen one as
an auxiliary window, and the fullscreen one stays; when fullscreen ends the
shown window takes its place.

The two-finger back/forward swipe asked the browser UI page for history,
which has none; it now goes to the active tab. The browser frame no longer
scrolls at all, so it never rubber-bands, without swallowing the swipe a page
passes up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
